## Post

Text from Article: I saw a number of complaints around Sol's inability to select appropriate subagents, which presumably is one of the main reasons OpenAI created Terra and Luna, although I'm not convinced you ever actually want to use Terra:
Claim: OpenAI created Terra and Luna as subagent models for Sol to select from.

## Your earlier research
The claim is mostly wrong. OpenAI released Terra and Luna as the lower tiers of the GPT-5.6 family, alongside Sol. They are standalone models, not models built to serve as Sol's subagents. OpenAI's own announcement says GPT-5.6 spans three tiers: Sol is the flagship, Terra is a lower-cost model with performance competitive with GPT-5.5, and Luna is the fastest and most affordable (https://openai.com/index/gpt-5-6/). Third-party guides describe the same thing: three independently trained and served models (https://www.cerebras.ai/blog/getting-the-most-out-of-gpt-5-6-sol-terra-and-luna and https://techjournal.org/openai-gpt-5-6-sol-terra-luna). Another source says the tiers replaced the older Pro/Mini naming scheme (https://kie.ai/blog/gpt-5-6-sol-terra-luna-deep-dive). Terra and Luna can be used as subagents under Sol. Cerebras says Terra can be a strong subagent when paired with Sol, which sets direction and hands off implementation (https://www.cerebras.ai/blog/getting-the-most-out-of-gpt-5-6-sol-terra-and-luna). A developer-forum bug report says Codex documentation presents Luna as a valid custom-agent model, though Sol and Terra parents had trouble spawning Luna children (https://community.openai.com/t/gpt-5-6-luna-is-advertised-for-custom-agents-but-rejected-by-sol-terra-multi-agent-v2/1389020). Subagent use is a feature of Sol's 'ultra' mode, which spawns subagents (https://fourweekmba.com/openai-gpt-5-6-sol-terra-luna-subagents-government/). I found no source saying OpenAI created Terra and Luna specifically so Sol could choose between them as subagents. The author hedges with 'presumably', so the claim is speculation. The subagent use is real, but calling it the reason these models were created is unsupported.

